# misra-c2012-12.1 (Advisory) -- per-line suppressions under D-004 partial
# deviation. See docs/qualification/MISRA_DEVIATIONS.md D-004 for the full
# rationale. Each entry below is a cppcheck/misra.py 12.1 hit on a line that
# falls inside D-004's accepted-as-implicit set: standard C precedence
# (`* /` over `+ -`, comparison over `&&`/`||`, member access over any),
# trivial null-check chains `(p != NULL && p->f != 0U)`, ternary mixed with
# arithmetic for tick-count or pixel-coord clamping, or a Doxygen comment /
# function signature line that the misra.py addon misattributes from a
# nearby expression. Adding redundant parentheses on every entry would only
# add noise -- the precedence is the one taught in K&R 2nd ed. section 2.12
# (table on p. 53) and is correctly understood by every static-analysis tool
# the project uses. Per D-004 risk assessment: net residual risk is
# acceptable for IEC 61508 SIL 3 / DO-178C DAL B given clang-tidy's
# mandatory-braces rule and the Phase 1 MC/DC coverage target.
#
